{
  "description": "Frozen accept/reject parity between the protocol validators and AppView's independent copy of the same wire rules (appview/src/shared/commerce/wire-rules.ts). Replayed by packages/commerce-protocol/__tests__/wire_rules_parity.test.ts and appview/tests/unit/commerce_wire_parity.test.ts. Both sides must agree on `valid` for every case.",
  "why": "AppView declares no @dina dependency and reimplements these rules. A hand-written copy of the §10.3 relationship vocabulary shared only two of seven entries with the protocol and nothing failed, because every commerce test happened to use one of the two overlapping names. Parity is asserted on BEHAVIOUR rather than bytes: the two implementations legitimately differ in structure (Zod schema plus gate vs. protocol validators), so accept/reject is the property that has to match, not the error text.",
  "scope_boundary": "`pack` internals are protocol-only. The unit vocabulary carries per-unit scales and canonical-decimal parsing, and AppView neither projects nor stores `pack` — search keys on identity, and orderability is settled by Core at quote and order time, which is the authority boundary. AppView checks that `pack.sell_unit` is present and an object so the record shape is sound, and these vectors carry no case that turns on a unit code or a decimal scale.",
